# Complete routing245 coverage publication design

This is an unexecuted packet-builder design for the exact current v3 family. It does not assert complete coverage. The existing v3 refinement proof is a three-unit success; the release gate below still requires every intended module. A later refinement must receive a separately reviewed successor design and manifest pin.

## Fixed family and release gate

Pin v3 `sources/generation.json` to `ca70be3402b6a0b1c33708970ac6400bcba7843382dd43e77fe09c9523e7db6b` and the executed v3 guard to `8b86edb49eb4bf9e8f82e6e5f10d012671a804bb4bd8743ab55d710bf3082ec5`. The family has 209 new units, 13 reused original batch units, one reused v2 cut43 unit, and three reused pilot units: 226 checked modules, 476 probes and 479 callers. The final source imports 248 project providers; its own fresh object is additional. These are explicit assertions, not fields inferred from a batch summary.

The builder accepts a final complete batch descriptor and its exact SHA, plus an independent final evidence receipt and its exact SHA. It recursively resolves the batch's explicit `prior_batches`, validates their manifest pins, and merges completed-unit records by module. Conflicting descriptors for one module are rejected. A failed earlier batch may contribute its actual completed successes; its failed record must remain separate. A successful selected-range batch is insufficient by itself. Require a terminal `PASS_COMPLETE_COVERAGE` batch, all 209 unique new-unit PASS records, the 17 exact reused records from the manifest, and the final `SitesRouting245` record. Require all 226 selected source/audit identities to match the frozen family and the final receipt's complete module-to-record index.

For every selected record, independently check PASS/non-prepare status, successful ordered source/audit commands, shared 120-second budget, `-j1 -M4096`, default proof limits, zero recorded and raw warnings, actual standard-axiom reports in exact audit order, caller census, source/audit snapshots, before/after identity, current input hashes, actual first providers, exact import DFS, and the fresh object saved before the audit and unchanged afterward. Three historical pilot records lack the later `preparation` field: allow that exception only for the three exact manifest-pinned pilot records and document it. Every production record, including reused v1 batches and cut43, must have its exact original `PREPARED_NOT_BUILT` receipt with no commands/fresh objects and correct inputs/providers. Do not synthesize missing historical fields.

Recompute the final 248-provider import closure from the selected source graph. Compare each selected ancestor's source/object pair to the provider pair used by the final proof. This binds both children of cut42 and every reused module to the actual final theorem. Require all current input hashes to remain identical after packet staging.

