## History, failures and incomplete attempts

Capture the complete UTF-8 contents under the original `coverage-production/` and `coverage-subtree-pilots/` scratch roots, excluding only compiled objects/cache files and clearly listed symlinks. The publication output must be fresh and outside both capture roots and the repository. Deduplicate by content hash, retain every original path as an alias, and check byte-perfect UTF-8 round trips. No `.olean`, `.ilean`, `.ir`, object files or cache symlinks are copied. Retain their paths, hashes, sizes and exclusion reasons as historical descriptors. Text snapshots inside proof-attempt directories are retained.

Require explicit preservation of the v1 unit013 source timeout (`59e6ab17...6a12`), v2 isolated cut42 non-timeout source failure (`e4c402e8...bab5`), cut43 actual PASS, v3 child/child/join records, and all source/guard versions. The v1 timeout is not reclassified as a semantic failure. The v2 diagnostic proves only that elaboration failed and pretty-printing encountered a recursion-depth error; it does not identify a deeper kernel cause. Retain initial metadata/emission errors and their separate corrected variants. Historical status labels remain unchanged.

Enumerate every batch record and every referenced attempt, not only selected successes. A batch with an active unit is an incomplete record, never final evidence. A referenced actual attempt must resolve to an exact verification record, or to an explicit evidence-based precompiler/no-record classification with all available outputs preserved. Unknown omissions reject the packet. For every historical verification record, check source/audit recorded hashes against preserved snapshots and raw command outputs against preserved logs. A nonselected source version may differ from today's source path; its exact historical bytes must still resolve through the alias registry. Preserve interrupted and failed attempts without promoting them into providers. Missing compiler objects may be described as unavailable historical objects only for nonselected attempts; selected current proof objects are mandatory at staging time.

The independent complete-review receipt may live outside both scratch roots. Capture that exact receipt and all its linked detailed receipts/reviewer scripts explicitly; do not assume recursive capture includes external evidence. The publication summary lists the exact reviewer roles, distinguishing source author reviews, root execution checks and independent existing-evidence checks.

## Reproduction and scope

Retain original guard/generator bytes as provenance. This design introduces no portable guard framework or dependency builder. The historical guards reference the exact cache/provider paths recorded during execution. The documentation must state that prerequisite honestly. The maintained Lean sources use normal imports and can be compiled in a provisioned environment; this packet itself does not certify a clean-checkout dependency rebuild.

The final checked proposition, once all gates pass, concerns all 6,460 leaves / 8,391 guards of the actual routed245 program and arbitrary instruction pointers, with fuel 4,000 and margin 64. It supplies the coverage premise for the separate runtime/blank-bootstrap endpoint. It does not itself establish the binary machine's blank halting equivalence, PA internalization, or any consistency theorem. Endpoint parent freezing must use the final actual record and recomputed dependency union; earlier 330/451/453 closure estimates are not proof evidence.

## Builder interface and root review

Proposed CLI: `build_packet.py --complete-batch PATH --complete-batch-sha SHA --complete-review PATH --complete-review-sha SHA --output FRESH_EXTERNAL_DIRECTORY`.

Implementation order: read and pin inputs; collect explicit successful-record graph; validate complete coverage and every selected binding; inventory every historical attempt; build an in-memory byte registry and map; write only the fresh output; round-trip all mapped bytes/history aliases; rehash selected input/provider identities; emit the final packet map last. No compiler, guard, emitter, simulation, download, Git or maintained write may occur. A failure before the map leaves a partial staging directory whose status is not publication-ready. Root independently reads the builder, executes it after complete coverage, verifies the map/history, installs exact files, and writes the separate maintained installation receipt.

The accompanying `contract.json` gives the concrete pins and future final-review schema. It is a design contract, not a fabricated final review or an executable proof guard.
